INT. MATTRESS SHOWROOM - NIGHT

Rows of beds under cold light. A tripod. A ring light. A laptop showing a chat window scrolling.

MARV QUIGLEY, 50s, polyester suit, headset mic, bounces on a king-size to show springs.

MARV
(to camera)
Folks, welcome to the Midnight Mattress Marathon!

A SECURITY GUARD, 30s, in a windbreaker, stands in the doorway with a flashlight. Marv doesn't see him.

MARV (CONT'D)
(to camera)
Three hundred viewers! That's a record, folks!

The guard coughs.

MARV (CONT'D)
(not turning)
Not now, Brenda.

SECURITY GUARD
I'm not Brenda.

Marv spins. He sees the flashlight. Drops to a sit.

MARV
Who the hell are you?

SECURITY GUARD
Mall security.

MARV
At a standalone store?

SECURITY GUARD
(shrugs)
It's a big parking lot.

MARV
(to camera)
Folks, ignore the man in the windbreaker.

The guard steps into frame. Waves at the camera.

SECURITY GUARD
Hi, Mom.

MARV
(muttering)
Oh, no.

SECURITY GUARD
I'm Darnell, by the way.

MARV
Darnell, you're ruining my numbers.

DARNELL
The chat says they like me.

MARV
(reading laptop)
"Who's the guard? Marry him." Okay. Fine.

Darnell sits on the next bed. He bounces. His face softens.

DARNELL
Wow.

MARV
Memory foam.

DARNELL
I could sleep here.

MARV
That's the idea, Darnell.

DARNELL
No. Like, tonight.

Marv looks at the camera. At Darnell. At the chat.

MARV
(to camera)
Folks, we're extending the marathon.

DARNELL
(to self)
Best shift ever.
